id: 37
hanzi: 阵
pinyin: zhèn
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Measure Word

meanings_summary:
  en: a wave; a spell; a burst of; brief period (wind, rain, applause); battle array
  es: racha; ráfaga; golpe; chaparrón; periodo breve; formación de combate

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Measure Word | Standard | classifier for events occurring in short bursts, waves, spells, or gusts | clasificador para rachas breves, oleadas o ráfagas | 一阵风 (a gust of wind)
  2 | Noun | Standard | battle array; front; position in military combat or struggle | formación militar; frente de combate; trinchera | 摆开阵势 (set out battle array)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 钻进刚被母亲晒过、铺得平平整整的被子里，鼻尖立刻涌上一阵阵混合着阳光与棉花香甜的暖意。 | Zuānjìn gāng bèi mǔqīn shài guò, pū de píngpíng-zhěngzhěng de bèizi lǐ, bíjiān lìkè yǒng shàng yí zhènzhèn hùnhé zhe yángguāng yǔ miánhua xiāngtián de nuǎnyì. | Slipping into the quilt freshly sunned and neatly made by mother, waves of sweet warmth blending sunlight and cotton immediately surged to my nose. | Al meterme en la colcha bien soleada y estirada por mi madre, oleadas de calor suave con aroma a sol y algodón envolvieron mi rostro.
  #2 | 报告厅内演讲刚一结束，全场听众便自发爆发出了一阵阵经久不息的热烈掌声与真挚欢呼。 | Bàogàotīng nèi yǎnjiǎng gāng yì jiéshù, quánchǎng tīngzhòng biàn zìfā bàofā chū le yí zhènzhèn jīngjiǔ-bùxī de rèliè zhǎngshēng yǔ zhēnzhì huānhū. | As the lecture concluded in the auditorium, the entire audience spontaneously burst into waves of prolonged enthusiastic applause and cheers. | Apenas concluida la conferencia, el auditorio entero rompió de forma unánime en sucesivas salvas de aplausos prolongados y vítores.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  一阵风 | a gust of wind
  一阵雨 | a shower / spell of rain
  一阵阵 | wave upon wave / repeated bursts
  掌声雷动 | thunderous applause in bursts
  上阵 | go into battle; take the field
  阵地 | battleground; position; bastion

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  冲锋陷阵 | chōng fēng xiàn zhèn | charge forward and breach enemy battle arrays; fight courageously
  严阵以待 | yán zhèn yǐ dài | remain in tight battle formation ready for the enemy
  临阵磨枪 | lín zhèn mó qiāng | sharpen spears on the battlefield; make hurried preparations at the last minute
  赤膊上阵 | chì bó shàng zhèn | strip to the waist and go into battle; throw oneself headlong into struggle

character_decomposition[1]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  阵 | zhèn | array; battlefront; spell of | formación; racha; oleada; frente | 阝 | mound / hill (left mound) | 阝 (defensive earthen rampart) | 车 (chē, war chariot / phonetic) | 6 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound where military chariots (车) align along an earthen defensive rampart (阝) in combat formations. | War chariots (车) deployed in orderly rows against a defensive hillside (阝), advancing in sudden coordinated waves. | Carros de combate (车) desplegados junto a una colina (阝) que avanzan en sucesivas oleadas tácticas. | 51 | NLKQ | 陣

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Chariots (车) lined up against the hillside rampart (阝) advance in sudden tactical waves and bursts (阵).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Carros de guerra (车) ordenados frente a la colina (阝) avanzan en oleadas y rachas coordinadas (阵).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Originating from the ancient art of warfare (八卦阵), '阵' transitioned from battlefield ranks into a temporal measure word capturing episodic bursts of nature—gusts of autumn wind or waves of nostalgia.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Pronounced in the 4th tone with a decisive falling pitch: 'zhèn' (51). When paired with '一' (yī), '一' shifts to 2nd tone: 'yí zhèn' (35-51).

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    陈 | chén | display; old; surname | Has 东 on the right of 阝 instead of 车
    车 | chē | cart; vehicle | Standalone right component of simplified 阵
    附 | fù | attach; close | Has 付 on the right of 阝 instead of 车
    阶 | jiē | steps; ladder | Has 介 on the right of 阝 instead of 车
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    阵雨 | zhèn yǔ | shower of rain
    阵痛 | zhèn tòng | labor pains; spasm; short sharp pain
    排兵布阵 | pái bīng bù zhèn | deploy troops in battle formations
    助阵 | zhù zhèn | cheer on; back up; support

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 阵 acts as a measure word for intermittent, wave-like, or temporary phenomena that surge and subside.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 阵 vs. 场 | cháng | 阵 classifies sudden, short-lived bursts of rain or wind (e.g. 一阵风, 一阵雨), whereas 场 classifies extended, complete events, shows, or prolonged storms (e.g. 一场大雨, 一场电影).
    2 | 阵 vs. 串 | chuàn | 阵 implies periodic waves surging and ebbing, while 串 emphasizes discrete physical items strung together along a single linear thread (e.g. 一串钥匙).
    3 | 阵 vs. 番 | fān | 阵 describes sudden physical bursts of sensations or weather, whereas 番 designates an extensive expenditure of mental or physical effort (e.g. 一番番苦心).

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 秋风乍起，卷起院角一堆金黄的落叶，在半空中打着旋儿。门缝里吹进一阵阵清凉的微风，伴随着远处隐约的笛声，给久居喧嚣都市的心灵送来了一阵难得的清宁与释怀。 | Qiūfēng zhàqǐ, juǎnqǐ yuànjiǎo yì duī jīnhuáng de luòyè, zài bànkōng zhōng dǎ zhe xuán'ér. Ménfèng lǐ chuījìn yí zhènzhèn qīngliáng de wēifēng, bànsuí zhe yuǎnchù yǐnyuē de dísheng, gěi jiǔjū xuānxiāo dūshì de xīnlíng sònglái le yí zhèn nándé de qīngníng yǔ shìhuái. | Autumn wind stirred, swirling golden leaves in the courtyard corner. Breezes blew through door cracks in waves, accompanied by distant flutes, delivering rare serenity and release to urban-weary souls. | El viento otoñal alzó remolinos de hojas secas en el patio. Por la rendija entraban oleadas de brisa fresca que, con el eco lejano de una flauta, trajeron un sosiego reconfortante al espíritu.
  #2 | 气象雷达监测显示，强对流冷锋过境引发了一阵阵剧烈的短时雷暴大风。防汛抗旱指挥部迅速启动应急预案，通过高频次气象卫星云图研判风暴走向，保障了沿海航运与电网设施的安全稳定。 | Qìxiàng léidá jiāncè xiǎnshì, qiángduìliú lěngfēng guòjìng yǐnfā le yí zhènzhèn jùliè de duǎnshí léibào dàfēng. Fángxùn-kànghàn zhǐhuībù xùnsù qǐdòng yìngjí yù'àn, tōngguò gāopíncì qìxiàng wèixīng yúntú yánpàn fēngbào zǒuxiàng, bǎozhàng le yánhǎi hángyùn yǔ diànwǎng shèshī de ānquán wěndìng. | Radar monitoring showed convective cold fronts triggering waves of violent short-duration thunderstorms. Flood control headquarters activated emergency plans, tracking clouds via satellites to safeguard maritime shipping. | El radar meteorológico detectó un frente frío que desató ráfagas violentas de tormenta. El centro de control analizó imágenes satelitales en tiempo real para proteger la navegación costera y las redes eléctricas.
